############################################################ # Body ############################################################
BEGIN_PGML One way to write down an Euler trail or circuit is to list the _edges_ in order. Each edge will be a pair of vertices, and to indicate what direction we travel over that edge, we can write it as an ordered pair rather than a set. For example, consider this graph:
>> [@image(insertGraph($image_1), width=>180, alt=>qq"a path of 4 vertices labeled a, b, c, d connected in that order by three edges.")@]* <<
There are two Euler trails we could write:
[``` (a,b), (b,c), (c,d) \qquad \text{or} \qquad (d,c), (c,b), (b,a) \text{.}```]
END_PGML
