BEGIN_PGML Write down an Euler trail for the graph below.
>> [@image(insertGraph($image_2), width=>240, alt=>qq"a graph with 6 vertices labeled a through f. Vertices a and f have degree one and are drawn on the far left and right respectively. The other vertices form a diamond. edges: (a,b), (b,c), (b,e), (b,d), (c,e), (d,e) and (e,f).")@]* <<
For each vertex, write down its degree and the number of times it appears in your list of edges.
>> [@DataTable( [ [PGML('vertex'), PGML('degree'), PGML('times listed'), ], [PGML('[`a`]'), PGML('[_]{1}{5}'), PGML('[_]{1}{5}'), ], [PGML('[`b`]'), PGML('[_]{4}{5}'), PGML('[_]{4}{5}'), ], [PGML('[`c`]'), PGML('[_]{2}{5}'), PGML('[_]{2}{5}'), ], [PGML('[`d`]'), PGML('[_]{2}{5}'), PGML('[_]{2}{5}'), ], [PGML('[`e`]'), PGML('[_]{4}{5}'), PGML('[_]{4}{5}'), ], [PGML('[`f`]'), PGML('[_]{1}{5}'), PGML('[_]{1}{5}'), ], ], align => '*{3}{l}', valign => 'middle',);@]* <<
END_PGML
